  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the provided images. My focus is understanding the visual layout and content of the ARIS application screens. I\'m noting key elements like data visualizations, input fields, and navigation, to get an early draft. This will form the core of the application\'s visual architecture.\n\n\n**Examining the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now closely examining the initial dashboard screen. The ARIS brand presence is clear with its neon accents against a dark backdrop. The daily timeline presents scheduled blocks with focus areas. The injury diagnostic features a body mannequin and key indicators. I\'m focusing on how the \"Critical Load\" card presents actionable info, and the \"Post-Match Protocol\" section is a focus for recovery guidance with a checklist.\n\n\n**Exploring Facility Options**\n\nI\'m now integrating facility options into the picture. I\'ve noted location-based facility cards, including walk-in and appointment-based options, all with \"BOOK NOW\" buttons. The focus is on incorporating this location data seamlessly into the user journey.\n\n\n\n**Reviewing Performance Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the latest performance data. I\'m noting the \"TEAM READINESS,\" \"INJURY RISK,\" \"HRV BASELINE,\" and \"OPTIMIZATION STATE.\" The \"MATCH READINESS RECOMMENDATION\" provides crucial insights. I\'m focusing on those cleared for play versus those needing caution. I\'m also analyzing the AI-generated recovery protocols across different sports. I\'m also examining the recovery scores and trends.\n\n\n**Assessing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI components. I\'ve noted a hydration index, a 7-day trend chart, and a \'View Full Dashboard\' button. The active \'Recovery\' section in the bottom nav is clear. I\'m moving on to Athlete Profile setup, specifically the sport selection screen and its discipline graphics. I\'m preparing a summary of the user\'s requirements to determine our approach.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 92659618
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
