  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Rejecting Firebase Integration**\n\nI\'ve discarded Firebase; the user explicitly wants a non-Firebase architecture. My current focus is implementing backend and frontend with an Express server, considering SQLite, file persistence, or an in-memory approach for data storage.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Specifications**\n\nI am now thoroughly examining the user\'s requirements, paying close attention to both the textual prompt and the provided images. The focus is now on extracting every detail to define the app\'s structure. The app needs to be real-time and fully functional, supporting user auth, survey logging, roster management, diagnostic tools, and AI recovery. I am carefully analyzing the images to derive insights, paying particular attention to the ARIS branding, the dark theme, and the key features and data displayed on the dashboard screen, which is the initial screen.\n\n\n**Defining App UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI components. Specifically, I am planning the daily timeline display, the injury diagnostic tool with the interactive body outline and hotspots, and the recovery plan section which includes a checklist. Each element is designed to be interactive with dynamic display for real-time app use. The plan is to create a sleek user experience, considering the provided dark theme and ARIS branding.\n\n\n**Detailing Recovery Session Design**\n\nI\'m now detailing the recovery session design based on clinical network and performance survey screens. I\'m focusing on the \"START RECOVERY SESSION\" button which is a big neon button that triggers a live guided recovery timer. The screen should also include a \"CLINICAL NETWORK\" section displaying nearby recovery locations with booking options. The performance survey screen, will collect biometrics such as sleep and hydration levels. I am currently considering the UI components for biometric input.\n\n\n**Designing Biometric Input**\n\nI am now designing the biometric input section, focusing on \"Low\" / \"High\" buttons or a level selector for general fatigue, along with a rating scale from \"EXTREME EXHAUSTION\" to \"FULLY REFRESHED\" using visual battery status cells. The action button will be labeled \"Submit Data (SECURE HIPAA-COMPLIANT TRANSMISSION)\" for immediate real-time updates to readiness and the dashboard.\n\n\n**Interpreting Match Readiness**\n\nI\'m now interpreting the \"MATCH READINESS\" data, focusing on the individual player recommendations and risk assessment. I am focused on the interactive flags for \"INJURY RISK\" and the \"AVG HRV BASELINE\". I am interpreting \"CLEARED TO PLAY\", \"CLEARED WITH CAUTION\", and \"NOT CLEARED\" data.\n\n\n**Defining Recovery Protocols**\n\nI\'m now detailing sport-specific recovery protocols. For hockey, I\'m noting lateral glute activation, wrist mobility, and sprint drills. Table tennis will focus on reflex-based drills and forearm stretches. I am currently considering an interactive AI protocol generator powered by a Gemini API to allow user customization of pre and post-match recovery.\n\n\\n\\n\nI am also working on Screen 5, the recovery score overview, including a circular gauge with a neon green arc to show the recovery score, and a status badge to provide more information. The screen will also have insights and metric cards for sleep and hydration. I\'ve also detailed a 7-day trend chart for the recovery score.\n\n\n**Specifying Sport Selection**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user sport selection. I am planning a grid of sport cards with rich icons and photos for Cricket, Football, Basketball, Running, Tennis, and Gym. A \"Continue\" button will follow. The design is intended to calibrate biometric data.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m now detailing authentication, and the backend. It will be an Express server with REST endpoints and SQLite or file-backed JSON database for users, surveys, athlete profiles, and bookings. I\'m planning real-time dashboard updates with WebSockets or Server-Sent Events, or a fast polling method, for responsiveness on mobile and desktop.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 680895810
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
