  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Full-Stack Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the structure of full-stack applications built with Express and Vite. The focus is on understanding the \"dev\" and \"build\" scripts, as well as configuration implications. I\'m taking a deep dive into how Vite handles frontend bundling and how the backend utilizes esbuild for server-side operations, particularly node-specific aspects.\n\n\n**Evaluating Dependencies for Auth**\n\nI\'m now exploring authentication and persistence options. I\'m trying to decide if I need external packages like `jsonwebtoken` or `bcryptjs`, or if I can write a clean auth module myself. I\'m also assessing the necessity of `better-sqlite3`, `cors`, or `cookie-parser`. I\'m leaning toward a simple JSON storage engine with atomic writes, a Gemini API proxy, and security features in `server.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining Core Tech Stack**\n\nI\'m now satisfied with the base tech choices. Using `node:crypto` seems perfect for auth and session tokens; no heavy native packages are necessary. The platform architecture for **ARIS** is being carefully designed. I\'m moving on to a detailed design specification.\n\n### App Concept & Design Specification\n**ARIS: Athlete Recovery & Performance Intelligence**\n\n**Brand Identity & Styling**:\n- **Palette**: Dark futuristic athletic aesthetic.\n  - Primary Background: `#0B0C0E` (deep matte onyx)\n  - Card Surfaces: `#13151A` (charcoal with `#1F232B` subtle borders)\n  - Accent / Brand Highlight: `#D2FF00` (High-vis neon volt/lime green)\n  - Critical / Risk: `#FF4B4B` (Warning red/rose)\n  - Caution / Moderate: `#FFB800` (Amber gold)\n  - Secondary Accents: `#3A86FF` (Hydration blue), `#A0AAB8` (Muted text)\n- **Typography**:\n  - Headings: Impactful uppercase condensed sans-serif (e.g., `font-sans uppercase tracking-tight font-black` or clean bold condensed styling like `Bebas Neue`)\n\n\n**Defining ARIS App UI**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user interface details for the ARIS app. I\'m focusing on the visual style, including the color palette and typography. I\'m choosing a dark, futuristic aesthetic with neon accents for high visibility. I\'m also considering typeface choices for headings and body text, keeping in mind readability and impact. I\'m also aiming for smooth animations and a clean, responsive layout.\n\n\n**Designing Athlete Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the main dashboard layout for ARIS, specifically the daily timeline and injury diagnostic features. I\'m prioritizing an intuitive design, incorporating interactive elements like a clickable 2D body outline for injury hotspots. The injury diagnostic panel updates dynamically based on user interaction, and provides critical load status indicators.\n\n\n**Developing Recovery Module**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the recovery session module for the ARIS app, which will integrate data on inflammation levels and a football-specific protocol. The recovery session is interactive, featuring toggleable tasks and a countdown timer. I\'m also including a clinical network feature with location-based clinic cards and appointment booking functionality.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Survey**\n\nI\'m now in the thick of designing the performance survey, screen two of ARIS. I\'m focusing on creating an intuitive multi-step form, incorporating interactive sliders and buttons for biometrics like sleep, hydration, and fatigue. The goal is to provide a seamless user experience for athletes to input their subjective data, which will then trigger dashboard updates. I\'m also ensuring HIPAA-compliant data transmission.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Risk Notifications**\n\nI\'m now implementing the roster risk alerts. I\'m building high-visibility cards for athletes at risk, including fatigue, sleep, and metabolic data. I\'m creating a roster table with filterable columns for athlete status and a clickable profile for in-depth data. Team stats like readiness and injury risk are also in progress. I\'m focusing on highlighting the most critical issues.\n\n\n**Implementing Roster Risk Alerts**\n\nI\'ve just added roster risk alerts, creating detailed cards for athletes. Now the app displays an athlete\'s availability using colored statuses: \"CLEARED TO PLAY\", \"CLEARED WITH CAUTION\", and \"NOT CLEARED\".  I am planning to expand this by integrating sports-specific AI recovery protocols.\n\n\n**Designing AI Recovery Protocol**\n\nI\'m now integrating an AI-driven recovery protocol generator, allowing users to specify sport, target muscle, injury state, and intensity. I\'m building a server endpoint to call the Gemini API, `/api/generate-protocol`, returning custom warm-up and recovery drills. The protocol will include exercise details and physiological impact.\n\n\n\n**Defining Profile and Auth Flow**\n\nI\'m now designing the athlete profile setup screen and authentication flow for the ARIS app. I\'m focusing on a clean sport selector grid with persistent authentication. There will be quick demo persona switches. I\'m working to make sure user data stays in local storage. Also, I\'m integrating email/password login and registration. This will validate via server-side endpoints.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 833870503
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
