  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing File Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on planning the project\'s file structure and database architecture. I\'m leaning toward a file-backed JSON database engine for its simplicity, with atomic writes to ensure data integrity. My goal is to auto-seed the database with realistic initial data upon startup, potentially using `data/db.json` to store everything.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously defining the data structures, considering athletes, biometric history (surveys), injury diagnostics, recovery protocol tasks, and appointments. I\'m focusing on attributes like IDs, names, email, passwords, roles, and status (CRITICAL, MODERATE, OPTIMAL), plus sport-specific details and health metrics. I\342\200\231m thinking how to properly implement the biometrics, like sleep data, hydration and fatigue level.\n\n\n**Outlining Booking Features**\n\nI\'m now outlining features for booking management. I\'ve defined data attributes like `id`, `userId`, `clinicName`, `distance`, `bookingType`, `date`, `time`, and `status`. I\'m also mapping attributes for timeline events, including `id`, `userId`, `date`, `timeRange`, `title`, `focus`, `category`, and a `isHighlighted` flag.\n\nI\'m starting to visualize the server API routes, considering endpoints for authentication, user dashboards, survey submissions, roster management with high risk alerts, booking appointments, and timeline activities. I\'m also planning an AI-powered recovery protocol generator using `@google/genai` Gemini.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 389838983
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
