  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have built the **ARIS (Athlete Recovery & Performance Intelligence)** application with complete full-stack functionality, data persistence, user authentication, and real-time biometric synchronization.\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n\n- **Full-Stack Architecture & Data Persistence**:\n  - **Express Server & REST API**: Configured custom backend in `server.ts` providing secure endpoints for authentication, biometrics submission, squad roster telemetry, clinical bookings, and AI protocol generation.\n  - **Database Engine**: File-backed JSON storage engine (`data/db.json`) maintaining user accounts, historical surveys, timeline events, recovery tasks, and appointment records.\n  - **Real-Time Synchronization**: Live polling updates metrics, high-risk flags, and team readiness across views instantly.\n\n- **Fidelity to Mockup Screenshots**:\n  - **Main Dashboard**: Features a **Daily Timeline** with highlighted workout slots, an **Interactive Injury Diagnostic** human body canvas with clickable hotspots (e.g. *Right Hamstring Critical Load* warning), a **Post-Match Protocol Checklist** with an interactive **Guided Recovery Timer**, and a **Clinical Network** booking engine.\n  - **Performance Survey**: Multi-step biometric input form capturing sleep duration, hydration index, heart rate strain zones, muscle soreness, and a 5-cell general fatigue battery scale.\n  - **Squad Roster & Coach Risk Dashboard**: Displays high-risk alerts (*Rohit, Sandeep, Bharath*), filterable squad roster, team readiness KPI cards, and match readiness clearance status.\n  - **AI-Generated Recovery Protocols**: Pre-built protocols for Football, Cricket, Badminton, Kabaddi, Hockey, and Table Tennis, alongside a live server-side **Gemini API** custom protocol generator.\n  - **Recovery Overview**: Features a 94 Recovery Circular Gauge, status indicator, and interactive 7-Day score trend chart built with Recharts.\n  - **Athlete Profile Calibrator**: Discipline selector for Football, Cricket, Basketball, Running, Tennis, and Gym."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
